commit(n,t,ds,ch,items,'The page develops the additive, scalar and multiplication identities obtained from the graded comparison u_* and its compatibility with products. The scalar-law header writes an ordinary x^p, while the ensuing computation ends in x^(p); the written discrepancy is retained. The pale lower annotation asks whether the comparison respects divided powers, and the black marginal question asks whether F Gamma^*(X) has a pd structure. The last diagram is unfinished: no bottom horizontal comparison is supplied, and a right-hand label has an unclosed parenthesis. The coefficient c_pq is consistently lower-case here. The total-degree exponents have the small crossed/looped star form seen earlier, including the overworked blue source exponent. H’s section title Gribouillis belongs to the editorial transition to the following leaf and is not source text on this image. Foot number 336.',hand=['The very small graded star can look like alpha: the blue comparison and its black marginal restatement use the same total Gamma notation as the top comparison. Every occurrence on this sheet was checked.','The lower pale line has abbreviated mult., not multiplicatif, and gradué with a descending g. H’s foncteur is not supported.','Here the combinatorial coefficient is a small c, consistently at all four occurrences; this does not retroactively replace clearly taller C on other leaves.'],notation=[('c_pq','Small open lower-case c in all four occurrences on this sheet.'),('Gamma^*','The tiny star can have a looped alpha-like outline; the blue source is overwritten.'),('underlined 1','Unit object is a handwritten 1 with a separate horizontal underline.')],abbr=[('mult.','multiplicatif'),('p.d.','puissances divisées'),('alg.','algèbre')],checks=[check('335-text-identities','Additive, scalar and multiplication computations transcribed; the scalar header’s plain exponent differs from the last line.'),check('335-text-pd-question','Compatibility with divided powers is explicitly left as a question, not asserted as proved.')],unresolved=[r'pale bien',r'pale respecte-t-il'])
